      "story": "Glorious Victory is a tempera-on-canvas painting by Mexican artist Diego Rivera, created in 1954. The painting addresses the 1954 Guatemalan coup d'état that the Central Intelligence Agency (CIA) backed to overthrow the democratically elected Guatemalan president Jacobo Arbenz. It is held at the Pushkin Museum, in Moscow.",
      "facts": [
